android-app/build/# Nadeem Mobile — Phone Lock System

Locks a customer's phone to a single "Locked by Nadeem Mobile" screen when
they miss an installment payment, and unlocks it again from your dashboard
when they pay. No calls, no other apps, until you unlock it.

This has three parts:
1. **android-app/** — the app installed on each customer's phone.
2. **server/** — the backend that stores your customers and sends lock/unlock commands.
3. **server/public/** — your dashboard (opens in any browser) to add customers and tap Lock/Unlock.

---

## Before you start — what this can and can't do

Please read this honestly, it'll save you trouble later:

- ✅ Blocks Settings → Factory Reset
- ✅ Blocks Safe Mode (a common trick to disable a locking app)
- ✅ Hides the power-button menu while locked, so there's no "Power off / Restart" option on screen
- ✅ If the phone is restarted anyway (e.g. battery died and it reboots), it **comes back locked automatically** — restarting does not bypass the lock
- ✅ Even a full wipe done outside Android (via recovery/bootloader mode with a PC) can be made to ask for your shop's Google account before the phone works again (Factory Reset Protection — see step 3)
- ❌ No software can stop someone from physically holding the power button to force a reboot, or opening the phone and removing the battery — that's hardware, not something any app controls. The point of the protections above is that **doing this doesn't help them** — the phone just comes back locked.
- ❌ This only works on **Android** phones. iPhones don't allow this kind of remote lock without Apple's business enrollment system, which isn't practical for a shop.
- ❌ This must be set up on the phone **before you hand it to the customer** (right after you buy/reset it) — it can't be installed remotely afterward without the customer's cooperation.

One important practical/legal point: keep this a clearly disclosed part of your
installment agreement — tell the customer their phone will be locked to
"Nadeem Mobile" if they miss a payment, and get that in writing when they buy.
That protects you if there's ever a dispute, and it's why the lock screen
shows your shop's name openly rather than hiding what's happening.

